  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "direct judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The primary declaration establishes conservative sequential execution. Its source correspondence must be assessed under Q10, which authorizes supplied geometry and flux data but does not explicitly remove the requirement that the directional operations represent the relevant numerical problems. Companion declarations support specializations without becoming conjuncts of the primary target.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 6, Section 1.3 describes extending one-dimensional high-resolution methods through successive coordinate problems. Q10 selects coordinate connectivity, supplied physical volumes, shared normal fluxes, and conservative updates. The primary type contains only cellVolume, rule, stages, state, and their algebraic operations."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The blind translation accurately reconstructs the primary declaration, including intermediate-state execution, volume normalization, telescoping, and whole-line dependence. The dispute concerns correspondence to the selected source claim rather than a translation error.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001-D006 expand to U(c)=u(c)-(dt/V(c))•(F(c successor)-F(c)) and a left fold. The blind translation reproduces these definitions and all four stage-specific conclusions."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined and accepted=false. The unresolved reverse semantic implication prevents an equivalent, stronger, weaker, or different classification from being established under the supplied comparison policy.",
      "primary_evidence": "The methodology requires separate implication decisions and preservation of unresolved uncertainty. The exact target fixes a bilateral lattice and positive-duration schedules, while neither the selected paragraph nor Q10 fully specifies their representational scope."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined independently of the direct judge's verdict. The reconstructed proposition has the same unresolved source correspondence as the exact declaration.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind dossier and translation quantify cells D→Z and arbitrary line rules, assume positive covering schedules, and conclude discrete execution and balance identities. Section 1.3 does not specify this complete mathematical domain."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D027 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve declaration meaning as understood: Int is the ordinary bilateral integer domain. Its source-match uncertainty belongs to applicability, not to uncertainty about the dependency itself.",
      "primary_evidence": "D027 supplies Int; D028 uses Int.add; D058 embeds Nat by Int.ofNat; D022 replaces coordinates. Together these give unrestricted integer lines without truncation or automatic periodic identification."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
      "resolution": "The binders and their effective domains are understood. The covering finite list forces D to be finite, and its nonemptiness forces D to be inhabited. E includes ordinary real vector states. Whether the full lattice represents the entire selected source grid class remains unclear.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target assumes stages:List(D×Real), stages≠[], and ∀d,∃dt,(d,dt)∈stages. Its cells are all D→Int. Printed page 6 imposes rectangular or logically rectangular grid structure without specifying a global index domain."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "Positive supplied cell volumes accord with Q10 and exclude zero-denominator artifacts. Nonempty directional coverage accords with an actual sweep. Strictly positive durations are an explicit forward-stage restriction; their full source applicability is not established and cannot count as stronger content.",
      "primary_evidence": "hvolume and hduration are strict inequalities. D005 divides dt by volume. Q10 supplies physical volumes but does not select a duration sign convention; the source gives no substep schedule."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "Separate harmless algebraic generality from unverified representation coverage. Arbitrary real modules and singleton direction sets do not exclude ordinary multidimensional instances. Full integer-product indexing and positive-duration schedules are specific representation choices whose coverage is unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "The primary type permits D=Fin 2 or Fin 3 and E=Fin m→Real. The Cartesian companion and cartesian_primary_instantiation retain integer-indexed axes and the same schedule premises."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Algebraic boundary cases are resolved: positive volumes avoid zero division, count=0 gives zero sums and equal endpoints, and actual stages admit prefix decompositions. Physical boundary handling remains unspecified. A total lattice alone does not prove bounded grids are excluded, but no boundary-compatible extension correspondence is supplied.",
      "primary_evidence": "Finset.range count indexes exactly count cells, with endpoint fluxes start and start+count. D003 consumes an entire integer line. Neither the primary type nor the companion types supply a finite-domain boundary extension."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "Correct the claim that companion admission definitions are unavailable: they are supplied in the complete inline dossier. They require each directional face problem to lie in the routine's domain at its actual intermediate state. This resolves their meaning, but does not establish admission for all source executions or numerical correctness of the returned information.",
      "primary_evidence": "FaceAdmitted unfolds to method.domain of adjacentCellRiemannProblem. StageAdmitted quantifies every cell. SweepAdmitted recursively requires StageAdmitted and admission of the suffix after the actual advance. RiemannInformationFluxMethod requires constant consistency but no PDE solution certificate or accuracy property."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation's abstract domains agree with the declaration. Supplied positive volumes are authorized by Q10; requiring every volume to be derived from a chart would exceed that convention. Global grid-domain coverage remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "Q10 explicitly selects supplied physical cell volumes and disclaims a book-supplied chart or Jacobian definition. The primary type takes cellVolume:(D→Int)→Real without a geometric realization predicate."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve volume positivity and directional coverage as compatible with the recorded interpretation. Preserve uncertainty only about the exact schedule and global-domain applicability; no fixed order, equal durations, or repetition count is imposed.",
      "primary_evidence": "hcover requires occurrence of each direction, List permits repetitions, and hduration requires positive second components. Section 1.3 specifies successive directional treatment without these additional schedule details."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C08 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve shared-face identity and state roles positively under Q10. A face indexed by its right cell has one value used with opposite signs in adjacent cells, and each stage reads its preceding output. Supplied physical roles need not be internally derived from geometry under this convention. They must not be confused with a certification of arbitrary rule values as physically appropriate.",
      "primary_evidence": "D002 uses normalFaceFlux at the successor minus normalFaceFlux at the current cell. D003 fixes the face index and reads its coordinate line. D004-D006 use prefix-produced states. CartesianGrid defines width products and transverse areas; areaWeightedRule explicitly multiplies the supplied flux by that area."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The measured Cartesian specialization is substantively represented, not merely named. It supports intended rectangular instances but supplies no general equivalence between the full integer lattice and every bounded or periodic logical grid. Retain that limited applicability uncertainty.",
      "primary_evidence": "CartesianGrid.cellBox uses products of actual half-open axis intervals; cellVolume is the product of positive widths; tangentialFaceBox uses transverse coordinates. The native Cartesian companion states the corresponding measure identities and equality with the one-dimensional flux-difference update."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "The theorem is nonvacuous in the intended dimension range, despite impossible premises for empty or infinite D. Degenerate segments are harmless. Boundary-extension semantics remain an independent unresolved issue.",
      "primary_evidence": "Take D=Fin 2, E=Real, V=1, stages=[(0,1),(1,1)], and rule(d,c,t,line)=line(c(d)-1). D001-D003 then give U(d,1,u)(c)=u(c[d:=c(d)-1]), which changes suitable nonconstant states while satisfying every premise."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The primary rule is total as an algebraic function; this neither requires nor proves existence of solutions to directional PDEs. The information specialization allows partial routines and requires admission throughout execution. There is no source well-posedness theorem here to reconstruct, but the bridge from arbitrary updates to the relevant numerical solves remains absent.",
      "primary_evidence": "The primary rule has no domain predicate. RiemannInformationFluxMethod.solve takes a domain proof, and guardedRule uses a fallback outside that domain. SweepAdmitted checks successive states rather than inferring later admission from initial admission."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication source_implies_lean unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve the conditional algebraic implication positively once the exact target representation is fixed: cell balance follows by cancellation, segment balance by telescoping, line dependence by coordinate replacement, and execution decomposition by the fold. Preserve uncertainty about the reverse semantic implication for the entire selected source claim; the identities alone do not establish representation coverage.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001-D006 and D020-D022 determine all these identities without inspecting the target proof. Section 1.3 and Q10 do not specify a full integer-product domain or the complete admissible schedule class."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation adds no independent obstacle: its formulas follow from the same fixed conservative representation. The remaining reverse-implication uncertainty is identical to the exact target's applicability uncertainty, not uncertainty about arithmetic or translation.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind translation's definitions of F, N, U, and T coincide with D003, D002, D001/D005, and D004/D006, respectively. Its segment endpoints and whole-line agreement premise match the elaborated target."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "no",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation, the target captures conservative coordinate connectivity, shared supplied fluxes, and successive execution. It does not establish the complete selected source claim that the operations represent the relevant one-dimensional numerical problems being solved. For unit volumes and a positive covering schedule, rule(d,c,t,line)=the real value of c(d) gives a flux difference of 1 and decreases every cell by t, while retaining every asserted balance and dependence identity. This shows that the target's properties do not themselves certify numerical-problem linkage. Universal quantification over rules is useful because appropriate methods can be instantiated; it is not itself a defect. The missing component is the correspondence between those instantiations and the source's directional methods. The information companion supplies conditional execution and constant consistency, not general numerical correctness, and does not enlarge the primary proposition."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation and after fixing the exact positive-volume integer-lattice update representation, all target conclusions follow algebraically from the supplied definitions. No additional accuracy or exact-PDE-evolution assertion is hidden in them. However, neither the printed passage nor Q10 fully establishes the correspondence of this global lattice and positive-duration schedule domain with the complete selected source claim. This is uncertainty about semantic representation and applicability, not a claim that the algebraic identities may be false. The source alone does not choose these conventions, and the available evidence does not justify silently narrowing the comparison to only the structural identities."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "Whether the selected comparison is intended to cover only conservative execution structure or also the source's linkage to the relevant one-dimensional high-resolution numerical methods; Q10 does not explicitly remove that linkage.",
    "Whether every intended bounded or periodic logical-grid execution has a compatible representation by the total integer-line rules used in this exact target.",
    "Whether strictly positive stage durations exhaust the intended schedule class for this selected claim.",
    "The printed paragraph itself leaves logical-grid geometry, directional equations, and substep scheduling unspecified; the recorded convention must remain separate from printed-source authority."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "incomplete-directional-method-correspondence",
      "evidence": "Section 1.3 characterizes a numerical construction using successive directional problems. D003 accepts an arbitrary line rule. The information companion requires admission and constant consistency, but its dependent Result type carries no required solution or accuracy certificate.",
      "impact": "The primary theorem certifies useful execution and conservation properties, but does not establish the full numerical-method correspondence needed for acceptance of the selected source claim."
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "unresolved-representation-coverage",
      "evidence": "Cells are all D→Int, rules consume total integer lines, and every stage duration is positive. The source and Q10 do not explicitly settle global boundary representation or this complete schedule class.",
      "impact": "Full semantic equivalence remains unestablished. Any eventual restriction of applicability must be stated explicitly and cannot be classified as genuine stronger content."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "companion-definitions-resolved",
      "evidence": "The complete inline dossier includes FaceAdmitted, StageAdmitted, SweepAdmitted, guardedRule, CartesianGrid geometry, and areaWeightedRule. The measure supplement identifies the real measure through normalized Haar and Stieltjes declarations.",
      "impact": "The direct judgment's assertion that the admission definitions were unavailable is superseded by the supplied evidence. The companions have meaningful conditional semantics, but provenance and specialization do not establish complete source correspondence."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "nonvacuous-conservative-execution",
      "evidence": "D004-D006 preserve list order and intermediate states; D002 shares each interface value; positive volumes permit cancellation. A two-direction unit-volume upwind-shift instance changes nonconstant real states.",
      "impact": "The theorem is not vacuous and its balances are substantive. Its exact equalities concern discrete operations, not exact multidimensional evolution or universal practical effectiveness."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "I inspected the attached primary-source rendering and the exact inline declarations, dependency inventories, blind translation, judgments, and supplement without tools or target-proof inspection. I did not independently recompute hashes. The disputed arithmetic, dependency meanings, shared-face identity, companion admission semantics, Cartesian specialization, and nonvacuity can be resolved from this evidence. The remaining issues concern the scope of source correspondence under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation. That interpretation authorizes supplied geometry and conservative execution but does not unequivocally replace directional numerical solves by arbitrary algebraic rules or establish all global-domain and schedule correspondences. Consequently, acceptance and a faithful-stronger classification are not justified; the unresolved reverse semantic implication requires undetermined."
}
